{"baseRefName":"main","body":"Complete proof of k603 in the primary source’s nondegenerate nested-confocal-ellipse setting. A per-edge focal antipedal-distance difference equals a fixed coefficient times vertical displacement, so closure makes the two ordinary-distance sums equal for every N. Includes unchanged proof and receipt plus a separate geometry/source audit with an independent unit-normal derivation: 17,364 author and 1,993 independent exact checks. No hyperbolic-caustic extension or individual-sum constancy claimed. Intended claimed_solved 2/5; novelty and human peer review unestablished. Parent coordinates the queue entry.","headRefName":"dot/math-5100032","headRefOid":"3d159f0a00d0bd7ff8d558d6fbc75af5094f7a35","isDraft":true,"mergeCommit":null,"mergedAt":null,"number":110,"state":"OPEN","title":"Elliptic billiards: independently reviewed focal antipedal k603 proof","url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/pull/110"}
